WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.080
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.780
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享独家幕后故事，

7
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.400
stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
这些故事只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你。

8
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室女士》。

9
00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.270
Oh, hey there.
噢，嘿，大家好。

10
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.510
Welcome, everyone, to this little bonus episode.
欢迎大家收听这期特别加更节目。

11
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.990
Just throwing a little episode out there on a Friday for you.
周五给大家送上一期小节目。

12
00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.850
Yeah, happy bonus Friday.
没错，加更周五快乐。

13
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:40.890
Okay, so, you know, earlier this week, we broke down the movie Speed, and we mentioned
好的，你知道，本周早些时候我们解析了电影《生死时速》，我们提到了

14
00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:46.170
how very excited we were to get to talk to someone who was in the movie, who was on the
能和电影里的一位演员，一位在巴士上的演员聊天，我们有多么兴奋。

15
00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:46.590
bus.
巴士。

16
00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:50.790
You know her as Dwight's babysitter from the dinner party.
你们认识她是《办公室》“晚宴”那一集里德怀特的保姆。

17
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.950
We know her as Beth Grant.
我们认识她是贝丝·格兰特。

18
00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:57.610
And we got to talk to her about her time on that bus.
我们有机会和她聊了聊她在巴士上的时光。

19
00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:58.830
That's right.
没错。

20
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.310
Beth Grant is here.
贝丝·格兰特来了。

21
00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:05.530
Our Speed fans will remember her as Helen, the nervous passenger who tries, you know,
我们的《生死时速》影迷会记得她是海伦，那个紧张的乘客，她试图，你知道，

22
00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.230
to get off the bus too early and does not go so well.
过早下车，结果不太好。

23
00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.030
No, she gets blown up.
没错，她被炸飞了。

24
00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:10.870
I know.
我知道。

25
00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:16.890
Well, we were super curious what life was like on that bus with Keanu and Sandra and the rest
我们超级好奇在巴士上和基努、桑德拉以及其他演员一起生活是什么样的，

26
00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:17.450
of the caSt.
演员阵容。

27
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.270
And you guys, Beth does not disappoint.
伙计们，贝丝绝对不会让你失望。

28
00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.750
She has great stories about her time on Speed.
她有很多关于拍摄《生死时速》的精彩故事。

29
00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:28.310
Yes, and you know, we thought about putting her interview in our Speed Breakdown, but
是的，你知道，我们曾考虑把她的采访放在我们的《生死时速》解析里，但

30
00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.370
frankly, it stands alone.
坦白说，这段采访值得独立成篇。

31
00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:30.770
Yeah.
没错。

32
00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.270
It is its own thing.
它有其独特的价值。

33
00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.690
We hope you enjoy it.
希望你们喜欢。

34
00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.970
So here it is, our conversation with Beth Grant.
那么，这就是我们与贝丝·格兰特的对话。

35
00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:43.260
Grant, here you are on Office Ladies.
格兰特，欢迎来到《办公室女士》。

36
00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.620
Yeah, there you are.
是的，你在这儿。

37
00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:45.480
I can see you.
我能看到你。

38
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.720
We are so excited to have you here.
我们非常高兴你能来。

39
00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:49.200
We're such big fans of yours.
我们是你的超级粉丝。

40
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.060
I mean, everyone that watches The Office knows you from Dinner Party.
我是说，所有看《办公室》的人都知道你在“晚宴”那一集里的表现。

41
00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:56.840
You are Dwight's babysitter and his date to the dinner.
你是德怀特的保姆，也是他去参加晚宴的女伴。

42
00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:57.780
Oh, my God.
天哪。

43
00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.040
How much fun did we have doing that episode?
我们拍那一集的时候有多开心啊？

44
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:00.980
I mean.
我是说。

45
00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:01.980
So much fun.
太开心了。

46
00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.380
It was so hard.
那真的很难。

47
00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.680
Well, for me, I really thought I was going to lose it a couple of times.
对我来说，我真的觉得有几次我快要笑场了。

48
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:07.980
I mean, big time.
我是说，非常严重。

49
00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:13.380
When I was at the door carrying the cooler, I had just worked with Steve in Loomis Sunshine.
当我拎着冷藏箱站在门口时，我刚和史蒂夫合作过《阳光小美女》。

50
00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.740
And so, you know, we knew each other a little bit.
所以，你知道，我们彼此稍微认识一点。

51
00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:22.840
And I don't know, I felt like he was really trying to get me because the things he was improvising
我不知道，我觉得他真的在针对我，因为他即兴发挥的那些内容

52
00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:23.500
at the door.
在门口。

53
00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.020
And I was so nervous because, you know, guest stars, you've guest starred.
我当时特别紧张，因为你知道，客串嘉宾，你也客串过。

54
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:28.920
I mean, you don't know.
我是说，你心里没底。

55
00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.000
It's not your team, you know, and you don't know.
那不是你的剧组，你知道，你什么都不知道。

56
00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.080
You don't want to be bad.
你不想表现得太差。

57
00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.880
And I was holding and he kept saying these things.
我当时正拿着东西，他一直说那些话。

58
00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.420
And I finally just went way down like this.
最后我实在受不了，就蹲了下去。

59
00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.640
And he said, oh, great.
他说，噢，太棒了。

60
00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:41.960
Now she's crying.
现在她哭了。

61
00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.540
Anyway, we were off to a good start.
总之，我们开局还算顺利。

62
00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.640
And it was just the most fun.
那真的是太有趣了。

63
00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.000
I love you guys so much.
我太爱你们了。

64
00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.720
It was a very, very, very special memory.
那是一段非常、非常、非常特别的回忆。

65
00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:52.760
It is.
确实是。

66
00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:57.100
I mean, you have to look at it from our point of view, too, which is that we're on the other
我是说，你们也得从我们的角度来看，当时我们就在

67
00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:02.300
side of the door and the door would start closed and it would just open on you holding
门的另一边，门刚开始是关着的，然后一打开，就看到你拿着

68
00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:05.300
a cooler, bringing a cooler to a dinner party.
一个冷藏箱，带着冷藏箱去参加晚宴。

69
00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.820
It was so hard not to laugh.
忍住不笑真的太难了。

70
00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:09.440
Giant glasses.
巨大的眼镜。

71
00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:10.240
Yes.
是的。

72
00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:14.580
Every time you nod on that, you had a beat.
每次你点头的时候，你都含着一块甜菜。

73
00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.380
I was eating, sucking on a beat.
我在吃，在吮吸一块甜菜。

74
00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.980
But, you know, rain cracked me up.
但是，你知道，雷恩把我逗乐了。

75
00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:22.680
And they, he kept grunting while he was eating his beats.
而且他，他吃甜菜的时候一直发出咕哝声。

76
00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:23.560
Yes.
是的。

77
00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:26.140
Both of us just love those beats.
我们俩都特别喜欢那些甜菜。

78
00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.540
He's going, mm, mm, mm, mm.
他一直在那儿，嗯，嗯，嗯，嗯。

79
00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.480
Like it's the best thing he's ever tasted.
就像那是他吃过最好吃的东西一样。

80
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:33.720
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

81
00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.400
But all of you guys were so funny.
但你们所有人都特别好笑。

82
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:40.000
It was just the most bizarre, demented episode, really.
那真的是最离奇、最疯狂的一集了。

83
00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.080
Steve sleeping on the little thing at the foot of the bed.
史蒂夫睡在床尾的小东西上。

84
00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:46.600
But her having, well, she had three bedrooms to herself.
但她拥有，好吧，她一个人有三个卧室。

85
00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:47.280
Yeah.
是啊。

86
00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:48.880
Exactly.
没错。

87
00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.120
Well, we are so thrilled to have you here today.
我们今天能请到你真是太激动了。

88
00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.460
And we are going to talk with you about your time on the movie Speed.
我们要和你聊聊你拍摄电影《生死时速》的那段时光。

89
00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:58.640
Yes.
好的。

90
00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.520
We are super fans of Speed.
我们是《生死时速》的超级粉丝。

91
00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.160
Can you believe that we're coming up on the 30th anniversary?
你能相信我们快要迎来30周年纪念了吗？

92
00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.520
I can't.
我不敢相信。

93
00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.960
30 years ago, you were on that bus.
30年前，你就在那辆巴士上。

94
00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.020
Isn't that crazy?
这难道不疯狂吗？

95
00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.920
See, it's really nuts that time goes by so quickly.
你看，时间过得这么快真是太疯狂了。

96
00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:15.360
My daughter was not yet one year old.
我女儿当时还不到一岁。

97
00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:17.940
It was the first job that I had.
那是我接的第一份工作。

98
00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.480
I was on a series when she was born.
她出生时我正在拍一部剧集。

99
00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:25.780
But it's very different to do a sitcom and to do a feature, you know.
但拍情景喜剧和拍电影是非常不同的，你知道。

100
00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:29.740
And I thought that all of the bus stuff would be CGI.
我本以为巴士上的所有场景都会是电脑特效。

101
00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.920
I didn't know we were going to be on a live freeway.
我不知道我们要在正在通车的公路上拍摄。

102
00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:39.640
And that my trailer was going to be, you know, a mile and a half, two miles.
而且我的拖车离拍摄现场有一英里半，甚至两英里远。

103
00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.620
And I wouldn't be able to see my daughter.
我根本见不到我的女儿。

104
00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.820
And I didn't want her stuck under a freeway, stuck in a, you know.
我不想让她被困在高速公路下，困在那种地方。

105
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.200
So it was a painful experience in that way, being away from her.
所以那段远离她的日子，真的是一种痛苦的经历。

106
00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.980
And, you know, I was still breastfeeding.
而且，你知道，我当时还在哺乳期。

107
00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.040
Too much information, I know.
我知道，这话说得太多了。

108
00:04:55.240 --> 00:05:02.960
But I would leave the house at 5.30 and drive, crying all the way, you know, leaving my baby asleep.
但我每天五点半就得离家开车，一路上都在哭，因为要把熟睡的宝宝留在家里。

109
00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.560
And then I wouldn't get home until 7.30 because we had, you know, 12-hour days.
直到七点半才能到家，因为我们每天要工作十二个小时。

110
00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:09.620
That's where did you pump?
那你在哪儿挤奶呢？

111
00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.420
In my little trailer.
在我的小拖车里。

112
00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:15.700
I mean, I would, it wasn't painful.
我是说，我当时……其实并不痛苦。

113
00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.800
It was painful at times.
有时候确实挺痛苦的。

114
00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.680
I couldn't wait for those breaks when we got to go back.
我总是盼着休息时间，好能回拖车去。

115
00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:24.380
But a lot of the time, we couldn't even go back to our trailers.
但很多时候，我们甚至没法回拖车。

116
00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.900
We were on the freeway with an umbrella.
我们就待在高速公路上，撑把伞。

117
00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:28.880
That was kind of it.
也就只能这样了。

118
00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:34.340
This was one of my big questions because, like, how did bathroom breaks work?
这是我一直很好奇的问题，上厕所怎么办？

119
00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.180
We used porta-potties.
我们用的是移动厕所。

120
00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:38.680
Oh, they would have, like, stopping points along.
哦，他们会在沿途设置停靠点。

121
00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.160
But they weren't those fancy little porta-potties.
但那可不是什么高级的移动厕所。

122
00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:44.200
There were construction workers literally on the 105.
105号公路上真的有建筑工人在施工。

123
00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.180
It hadn't quite opened.
当时公路还没完全开通。

124
00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:47.020
It was live.
但已经通车了。

125
00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.780
There were, you know, construction workers, cars going by and so on.
你知道，有建筑工人，有来往的车辆等等。

126
00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:52.580
And there were real construction workers.
而且那是真正的建筑工人。

127
00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.780
And so they had to have porta-potties.
所以他们必须有移动厕所。

128
00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:57.880
So I think our porta-potties, they probably just incorporated them.
我想我们的移动厕所，大概就是直接借用了他们的。

129
00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:58.380
Okay.
好吧。

130
00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:02.260
So other than porta-potties, there was really nothing there.
所以除了移动厕所，那里真的什么都没有。

131
00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.480
Everything we see, the film crew added, right?
我们看到的一切都是剧组后来加进去的，对吧？

132
00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:11.100
We had 300 cars that were extras cars, which let me tell you something.
我们有300辆群众演员的车，我跟你说。

133
00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:17.560
You don't want to miss a line when they have to turn around 300 cars.
当他们需要调动300辆车时，你可千万不能忘词。

134
00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:24.440
But it was just one of those things, knowing that there are helicopters going around and 300 cars.
但这就是那种情况，你知道周围有直升机盘旋，还有300辆车。

135
00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:27.500
And Yon-de-bot, you know, love him, maniac.
还有扬·德·邦特，你知道的，我很喜欢他，但他是个疯子。

136
00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.920
And, you know, he's got all this stuff going on.
而且，你知道，他同时在忙各种事情。

137
00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.640
I mean, we were shooting with 11 cameras.
我是说，我们当时用了11台摄像机在拍摄。

138
00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:38.480
We had cameras on the wheels, you know, cameras all over the bus.
我们在轮子上装了摄像机，你知道，巴士上到处都是摄像机。

139
00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:39.120
We had cameras.
到处都是摄像机。

140
00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:40.540
I mean, crazy.
我是说，太疯狂了。

141
00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:46.920
But one time, to my mortification, I have, you know, quite an angular face.
但有一次，让我感到非常尴尬的是，你知道，我的脸型棱角比较分明。

142
00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.400
And it was Sandy's close-up.
当时正在拍桑德拉的特写。

143
00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:52.280
And my nose apparently kept popping in and out.
结果我的鼻子好像总是不停地进出画面。

144
00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:54.660
My nose and my chin.
我的鼻子和下巴。

145
00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:59.120
And finally, they had to stop 300 cars, turn around.
最后，他们不得不停下300辆车，重新调头。

146
00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.900
I mean, it's like, it wasn't subtle when you messed up.
我是说，一旦你搞砸了，那动静可一点都不小。

147
00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:03.880
It was not.
确实不小。

148
00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:05.380
Everybody knew.
所有人都知道了。

149
00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:08.900
And you could hear, going again, going again, turn around, turn around.
你能听到扩音器里喊着：再来一次，再来一次，调头，调头。

150
00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.180
It was horrible.
那感觉太糟糕了。

151
00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.040
But we made it.
但我们还是成功了。

152
00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:14.380
And we didn't mess up too much, you know.
而且我们没搞砸太多，你知道的。

153
00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:16.200
Well, I have a question for you, Beth.
好吧，贝丝，我有个问题想问你。

154
00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.600
What was the audition process like?
试镜过程是怎样的？

155
00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:20.980
Like, what was the scene you auditioned with?
比如，你试镜时演的是哪一场戏？

156
00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:24.220
And it seems like you didn't know you were going to be on an actual bus.
而且看起来你当时并不知道自己真的要在公交车上拍戏。

157
00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:25.680
I didn't.
我确实不知道。

158
00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:27.860
Well, it was John DeBond.
嗯，那是约翰·德邦德。

159
00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:33.760
And I had worked with him before on Flatliners that Joel Schumacher directed.
我之前和他合作过乔尔·舒马赫执导的《灵异空间》。

160
00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:39.000
And so I knew he was really a great DP.
所以我知道他是一位非常出色的摄影指导。

161
00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:42.040
You know, of course, he had done Die Hard, big, big movies.
你知道，当然，他还拍过《虎胆龙威》这种大制作电影。

162
00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.340
But I liked him.
但我很喜欢他。

163
00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:44.640
You know, he's crazy.
你知道，他这人很疯狂。

164
00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:45.720
I mean, he's like me.
我是说，他跟我很像。

165
00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:46.660
He's like, whirr.
他就像个陀螺一样，转个不停。

166
00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:50.380
In fact, Sandy, he and Sandy and I really had fun.
事实上，桑迪，他和桑迪还有我，我们真的玩得很开心。

167
00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:54.080
I think we probably drove people crazy because we cracked a lot of jokes.
我想我们可能把大家都搞疯了，因为我们老是开玩笑。

168
00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:57.020
And we were naughty, Sandy and I, quite often.
而且我和桑迪经常调皮捣蛋。

169
00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:00.640
And so the three of us got along really great.
所以我们三个相处得非常融洽。

170
00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:03.320
But anyway, so the audition process.
但不管怎么说，关于试镜过程。

171
00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:05.560
And it was John.
当时是约翰负责。

172
00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:09.120
And I read the script and I thought, a bus?
我读了剧本，心想，公交车？

173
00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:12.380
You know, going 50 miles an hour?
你知道，以50英里的时速行驶？

174
00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.660
It just seemed preposterous to me.
这在我看来简直荒谬透顶。

175
00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:18.700
And I called my friend Don Mancini, who wrote the Child's Play movies.
于是我打电话给我的朋友唐·曼奇尼，他写过《鬼娃回魂》系列电影。

176
00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.320
And Don, we were very close at that time.
那时候我和唐关系非常亲密。

177
00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:24.140
And he really knew Hollywood.
他真的很了解好莱坞。

178
00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.220
I mean, he knew what movies were happening.
我是说，他知道哪些电影正在筹备。

179
00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:27.340
He read all the scripts.
他读过所有的剧本。

180
00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:31.140
He had a real good sense of what was going to happen, what wasn't going to happen.
他对于什么会火、什么不会火有着非常敏锐的直觉。

181
00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:32.420
So I called him.
所以我给他打了电话。

182
00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.220
I said, you know, I've got this audition.
我说，你知道，我有个试镜机会。

183
00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:35.220
What do you think?
你觉得怎么样？

184
00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:36.660
He said, oh, do it.
他说，哦，去吧。

185
00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:36.980
Do it.
去试镜吧。

186
00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:37.780
It's a huge movie.
这会是一部大制作电影。

187
00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:38.600
It's going to be huge.
它一定会大火的。

188
00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:39.680
I said, really?
我说，真的吗？

189
00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:41.340
People want to watch a runaway bus?
人们会想看一辆失控的公交车吗？

190
00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:42.020
Absolutely.
绝对会。

191
00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:42.820
Do it.
去吧。

192
00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:43.100
Do it.
去试镜吧。

193
00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:46.860
So I read the script, which was not the script you saw, by the way.
所以我读了那个剧本，顺便说一下，那并不是你们后来看到的那个版本。

194
00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:48.100
Different script.
剧本完全不同。

195
00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:52.480
Graham Yeo's script was very different after Joss Whedon did the rewrite.
格雷厄姆·约的剧本在乔斯·韦登重写之后有了很大的变化。

196
00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:55.100
Yeah, that's what we're learning.
是啊，我们现在也才了解到这一点。

197
00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:58.840
And it's a lot of fun stuff that changed, you know.
而且有很多有趣的内容都改动了，你知道的。

198
00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:01.760
But it was a really nice role at that time.
但在当时，那确实是一个非常不错的角色。

199
00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:03.580
It wasn't what ended up being in the script.
它和最终出现在剧本里的样子并不一样。

200
00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:07.260
But it was sort of like the Poseidon Adventure or Towering Inferno.
但它有点像《海神号遇险记》或《火烧摩天楼》那种风格。

201
00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:09.680
We all had these backstories and history.
我们都有各自的背景故事和过往经历。

202
00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:11.420
And I liked my character.
而且我很喜欢我的角色。

203
00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:12.800
She had just gotten engaged.
她刚订婚。

204
00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:14.360
She had a little dog.
她有一只小狗。

205
00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:18.380
She and Sandy's character were friends.
她和桑迪的角色是朋友。

206
00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.740
I had been to see her do stand-up the night before.
前一天晚上我还去看过她的单口喜剧表演。

207
00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:24.160
So it was all, you know, chatty.
所以当时大家聊得很投机。

208
00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.900
And then every bus stop, they would stop.
然后每到一个公交站，车都会停下来。

209
00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.480
And the people would come on.
人们会陆续上车。

210
00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:31.020
And you would kind of find out more about them, you know.
你会逐渐了解他们更多的情况，你知道的。

211
00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:34.620
And so that was the script that I read.
这就是我读到的剧本。

212
00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:39.020
And so anyway, I just cut loose and had fun.
总之，我当时彻底放开了，玩得很开心。

213
00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.860
And in the script, I was the hero.
在那个剧本里，我是英雄。

214
00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:44.280
The bus driver actually had a heart attack in that script.
剧本里公交车司机真的心脏病发作了。

215
00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:49.080
And I was the one that came forward and did CPR and saved his life.
而我挺身而出，做了心肺复苏，救了他的命。

216
00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:55.320
And then I was the one who volunteered to get off the bus first to sort of test the waters.
然后我还是第一个主动提出下车去探探情况的人。

217
00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.140
And we did all that.
我们把这些都演了一遍。

218
00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.260
And I got on my knees in the audition.
试镜的时候，我跪在地上。

219
00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.540
And I was doing CPR.
我在做心肺复苏。

220
00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:01.680
I mean, I just went for it.
我是说，我真的全力以赴了。

221
00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.020
So it was really fun.
所以过程真的很有趣。

222
00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:04.200
And I really loved it.
我真的很喜欢。

223
00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:07.380
And I really, you know, hoped I would get it by the time I left.
离开的时候，我真心希望能拿到这个角色。

224
00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:16.920
And, but then, as it happens in Hollywood, we were shooting like the day after Labor Day.
但正如好莱坞常有的那样，我们在劳动节后的第二天就开始拍摄了。

225
00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:25.340
And we went to, we had a reading, table read, and we had a costume parade.
我们去参加了剧本围读，还进行了服装试装。

226
00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:33.740
And so first I get there and your boyfriend, Keanu, sitting there all pumped up, baby.
我刚到那儿，就看到你男朋友基努坐在那儿，浑身肌肉紧绷，宝贝。

227
00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.340
I mean, he looked good.
我是说，他看起来状态很好。

228
00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.840
And I was already a fan of his.
我本来就是他的粉丝。

229
00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:40.620
I'd always thought, to me, he's underrated, underestimated.
我一直觉得，在我看来，他被低估了，被小看了。

230
00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:42.620
I just think he's a genius.
我觉得他是个天才。

231
00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:46.980
He's so authentic and real and loving.
他非常真实、纯粹且充满爱心。

232
00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:48.640
And it always comes across.
而且这些特质总是能传达出来。

233
00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:52.820
Anyway, he's sitting there all pumped up, which I had never seen him like that.
总之，他坐在那儿，浑身肌肉紧绷，我以前从没见过他那样。

234
00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:54.940
And I said, oh, wow, you look great.
我说，哇，你看起来棒极了。

235
00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:56.540
This is really exciting.
这真的很令人兴奋。

236
00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.120
This is really good for you, huh?
这对你来说真的很棒，对吧？

237
00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:00.200
And he said, I hope so.
他说，希望如此。

238
00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.280
I mean, he's just so real.
我是说，他就是这么真实。

239
00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.980
So anyway, then we go in.
总之，然后我们进去了。

240
00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.000
So we get these new scripts.
我们拿到了新剧本。

241
00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:09.180
So I start going through the script.
我开始翻看剧本。

242
00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:11.280
And I said, huh, huh.
我心想，嗯？嗯？

243
00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.280
Out of the table read.
在围读的时候。

244
00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:14.780
It's the first time you've seen it.
这是你第一次看到剧本。

245
00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:17.880
The first time I've seen the rewrites, I think they were hot off the press.
这是我第一次看到修改后的剧本，我想它们刚打印出来不久。

246
00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.440
And I think, oh, my God, it's all her characters gone.
我心想，天哪，她的角色全没了。

247
00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:22.300
There's no dog.
没有狗了。

248
00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:23.480
I'm not engaged.
我没订婚了。

249
00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:24.580
I'm not friends with.
我也不再是她的朋友了。

250
00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:26.760
I thought, there's nothing here to do.
我心想，这儿什么戏份都没了。

251
00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:27.120
I don't know.
我不知道。

252
00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:27.880
What am I going to do?
我该怎么办？

253
00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:31.340
And so Sandy and I went to the same college.
桑迪和我上的是同一所大学。

254
00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.900
And she, obviously, younger than me.
她显然比我年轻。

255
00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:40.840
And when we had, they put out this directory of all the famous alumni, you know.
当时他们出了一本名校友名录，你知道的。

256
00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:45.200
And so I had a very nice little picture, a little nice bio.
我有一张很不错的照片和一段简短的个人简介。

257
00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:51.380
And then Sandy had this huge spread in the middle because she had done Working Girl, the series.
而桑迪在中间占了很大篇幅，因为她当时拍了《上班女郎》系列剧。

258
00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:54.460
And I thought, who the hell is that, you know.
我心想，这人到底是谁啊。

259
00:11:54.660 --> 00:12:00.160
And this guy that wrote for the Raleigh Newsom Observer said, oh, you need to meet her.
有个给《罗利新闻观察家报》写稿的人说，噢，你一定要见见她。

260
00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:00.980
You're going to love her.
你会喜欢她的。

261
00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:01.680
She's great.
她很棒。

262
00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:04.720
And gave me her phone number and said, call her up.
他给了我她的电话号码，让我打给她。

263
00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:05.740
Y'all will get along great.
你们一定会相处得很好。

264
00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.040
And I'm saying, I'm going to call her.
我当时想，我才不要打给她。

265
00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:10.880
I was jealous.
我嫉妒了。

266
00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:12.960
But anyway, so we're sitting there.
但不管怎样，我们当时坐在那儿。

267
00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:13.960
I just read this script.
我刚读完这个剧本。

268
00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:18.780
And in walks Sandra Bullock, the girl from my college.
然后桑德拉·布洛克走了进来，就是我大学里的那个女孩。

269
00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:22.420
And I was like, and then she turned.
我当时心想，然后她转过身来。

270
00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:24.400
And this really happened.
这事儿真的发生了。

271
00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:25.440
It makes me cry.
想到这儿我就想哭。

272
00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:28.320
She turned and she looked at me.
她转过身看着我。

273
00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:30.220
And her eyes lit up.
她的眼睛亮了起来。

274
00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:31.220
Her face lit up.
她的脸庞焕发光彩。

275
00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.760
And I fell in love.
我坠入爱河了。

276
00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:40.940
So Sandy comes over and she, you know, she's East Carolina, East Carolina, you know, Southern girl.
桑迪走过来，你知道的，她是东卡罗莱纳大学的，典型的南方女孩。

277
00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:44.940
So, you know, we were best friends for the whole shoot.
所以，整个拍摄期间我们都是最好的朋友。

278
00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:50.780
And she saved my life because I had just read this script where my part was kind of gone.
她救了我的命，因为我刚读完剧本时，发现我的戏份几乎被删光了。

279
00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:56.360
And then when we got on the set, well, we went to rehearse firSt.
后来我们到了片场，嗯，我们先进行了排练。

280
00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:57.640
Then we read the script.
然后我们读了剧本。

281
00:12:57.820 --> 00:12:58.540
She was fabulous.
她表现得太棒了。

282
00:12:58.860 --> 00:12:59.780
It was fabulous.
那真是太棒了。

283
00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:00.840
It was different.
那感觉很不一样。

284
00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:04.060
It wasn't what I wanted to do, but it was great.
虽然不是我想演的那样，但效果很好。

285
00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:05.740
We had the reading.
我们进行了剧本围读。

286
00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:08.280
Then we went for our costume parade.
然后我们去试了服装。

287
00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:09.960
And we did that.
我们完成了这些工作。

288
00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:13.120
And then we got on the set.
接着我们到了片场。

289
00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:14.560
We put, they put us on a bus.
他们把我们送上一辆巴士。

290
00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:18.800
And we went to the 105 freeway for the rehearsal.
我们去了105号高速公路进行排练。

291
00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.460
And I'm looking around.
我四处张望。

292
00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:23.500
Wait, the rehearsal was on a moving bus as well?
等等，排练也是在行驶的巴士上进行的吗？

293
00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:24.980
Yeah.
是的。

294
00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:27.600
I mean, you rehearsed on a moving bus.
我是说，你们是在行驶的巴士上排练的。

295
00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:28.420
Yes.
是的。

296
00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.220
But we didn't go 50.
但我们没开到50英里时速。

297
00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:31.000
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

298
00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.300
Maybe we did for a minute.
也许有一会儿开到了。

299
00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:33.240
They were testing that.
他们当时在测试那个。

300
00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:34.820
But mostly, yeah, we did.
但大部分时间，是的，我们确实是在上面排练的。

301
00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:36.020
Wow.
哇。

302
00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:36.660
Yeah.
是啊。

303
00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.700
And then we would all get out.
然后我们就会全部下车。

304
00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:40.400
Did anyone get car sick?
有人晕车吗？

305
00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:41.960
Oh, what a funny question.
噢，真是个有趣的问题。

306
00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:43.320
Not that I know of.
据我所知没有。

307
00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.100
Not that I know of.
据我所知没有。

308
00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:45.740
We did not.
我们没有。

309
00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.180
Maybe it's different on a bus than in a car.
也许坐巴士和坐小汽车感觉不一样吧。

310
00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:50.980
Maybe we're too scared.
也许是我们太害怕了。

311
00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:52.440
That's lucky, though.
不过那很幸运。

312
00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:53.220
That's lucky.
那很幸运。

313
00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:59.220
Would you guys actually be in the bus when the bus was hitting things?
当巴士撞到东西的时候，你们真的在车上吗？

314
00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:00.480
Oh, yeah.
噢，是的。

315
00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:04.900
So you would crash into cars while you were in the bus?
所以你们在巴士上的时候，它会撞上其他车？

316
00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:05.600
We did.
是的，我们撞过。

317
00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:06.880
I mean, sometimes, yes.
我是说，有时候是这样。

318
00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:07.580
Sometimes, though.
不过只是有时候。

319
00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:09.020
And I can't tell you which ones.
我不能告诉你具体是哪几次。

320
00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:11.600
But we were in it for a lot of it.
但大部分时间我们都在车上。

321
00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:12.200
You know?
你懂的吧？

322
00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:16.340
You know, like that one where we hit all the water things, you know?
你知道，就像我们撞到那些水桶的那次，你懂吗？

323
00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:17.060
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

324
00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:18.600
We were in the bus for that.
拍那场戏时我们就在巴士上。

325
00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:21.480
That was shot in Long Beach on an entrance.
那是在长滩的一个入口处拍的。

326
00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:22.660
And boom, boom, boom.
然后砰、砰、砰。

327
00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:25.940
And a lot of it was very real.
而且很多都是非常真实的。

328
00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.440
On the street, you know, with the baby carriage going.
在街上，你知道，还有婴儿车经过。

329
00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:30.380
We were all right there.
我们当时就在那儿。

330
00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:32.020
It was scary.
那很吓人。

331
00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:34.280
I mean, Jan is a nut.
我是说，简是个疯子。

332
00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.340
He likes to go for it.
他喜欢来真的。

333
00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.560
And fortunately, Sandy and Keanu and I are nuts.
幸运的是，桑迪、基努和我也是疯子。

334
00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:45.880
And, you know, Keanu did that stunt getting out of the jag onto the bus, you know.
而且，你知道，基努完成了那个从捷豹车跳到巴士上的特技，你懂的。

335
00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:46.120
Yeah.
是啊。

336
00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:47.520
His sister on doing it.
他妹妹也想做。

337
00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:57.240
And once he did his stunt, then, of course, Hawthorne James wanted to do his getting on the – and so I said, well, I'm not going to let men do theirs.
他做完特技后，霍桑·詹姆斯当然也想做他那个上车的动作，所以我说，好吧，我可不能让男人们抢了风头。

338
00:14:57.280 --> 00:14:58.440
I'll do mine.
我也要亲自上阵。

339
00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:00.360
Here I am a new mother.
当时我还是个新手妈妈呢。

340
00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.700
I mean – and they had stunt women for me.
我是说——他们其实为我准备了替身演员。

341
00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:07.500
They had, you know, two different stunt women there.
他们在那儿安排了两个不同的特技替身。

342
00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:11.920
They had – I had to do full-body cast, so they had three or four of me.
他们——我得做全身石膏模型，所以他们做了三四个我的替身。

343
00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:13.940
I mean, I was everywhere, you know.
我是说，我到处都是，你懂的。

344
00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:33.950
Okay, we really want to ask you about that hard right turn when the bus has the 90-degree turn and he's like, everyone, get on the other side.
好的，我们真的很想问问那个急右转的镜头，就是巴士90度转弯，他说“大家，都到另一边去”。

345
00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:36.510
And it goes up on two wheels.
然后车身就用两个轮子行驶。

346
00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:40.190
Like, were you on that bus when it did the hard right turn?
在那场急右转的戏里，你们在车上吗？

347
00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:42.250
We were, but I don't know.
我们在，但我不太确定。

348
00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:46.310
The two-wheel thing might have been shot as a separate piece.
两个轮子行驶的那部分可能是单独拍摄的。

349
00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:48.030
We did it, though.
不过我们确实拍过那个动作。

350
00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:53.410
So, it was right there at the entrance of the 105 and the 110, I believe.
我想那是在105号公路和110号公路的入口处拍的。

351
00:15:54.110 --> 00:16:01.490
So, it wasn't actually – I think it was on a street rather than the actual ramp, I think.
所以，其实并不是——我觉得那是在街道上，而不是在真正的匝道上，我是这么认为的。

352
00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:03.570
That's what it looks like.
看起来确实是这样。

353
00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:03.970
Yeah.
没错。

354
00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:07.890
It was – yeah, it's real.
那是——对，那是真实的。

355
00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:09.270
So much of it is real.
很大一部分都是真实的。

356
00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:13.630
What Jan said to me, I wanted to quit when I saw that we were shooting on the freeway.
简（Jan）跟我说过，当我看到我们要在那条高速公路上拍摄时，我当时想退出。

357
00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:17.750
And he said, trust me, I'm going to shoot this like a European film.
但他对我说，相信我，我会用拍欧洲电影的方式来拍这一段。

358
00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:20.470
You saw all the costumes were in earth tones.
你看到了，所有的服装都是大地色系的。

359
00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:26.670
And he said, we're going to cover this in a very specific way like a European film.
他说，我们要用一种非常独特的方式来呈现，就像欧洲电影那样。

360
00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:28.230
And real.
而且要真实。

361
00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:30.390
We're going to keep it real.
我们要保持真实感。

362
00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:33.730
And so, I took him at his word.
所以，我选择相信他的话。

363
00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:35.470
And I think that is what he did.
我觉得他确实做到了。

364
00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:36.010
Do you agree?
你同意吗？

365
00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:37.150
Yeah.
同意。

366
00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:41.730
I am blown away by some of these shots that they got and where the cameras were mounted.
他们拍到的一些镜头以及摄像机的安装位置，真的让我感到震撼。

367
00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:48.070
And I was so tense in so many scenes because it feels so scary.
在很多场景里我都感到非常紧张，因为那种感觉太真实、太吓人了。

368
00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:49.350
Yeah.
没错。

369
00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:49.930
Yeah.
是啊。

370
00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:52.310
It is – it was real.
那是——那确实是真实的。

371
00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:54.990
Anything you saw on our faces was probably real.
你们在我们脸上看到的任何表情，可能都是真实的。

372
00:16:57.210 --> 00:17:02.710
I have to imagine you guys really bonded being on the bus together for so long.
我能想象你们在公交车上待了那么久，一定建立了深厚的感情。

373
00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.430
I mean, how many weeks were you shooting?
我是说，你们拍了多少周？

374
00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:06.410
Well, I shot for six weeks.
嗯，我拍了六周。

375
00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:09.570
I think they shot for seven or eight after I died.
我死后他们好像又拍了七八周。

376
00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:11.590
Although Sandy had me come back.
不过桑迪（Sandy）让我回去补拍了。

377
00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:12.390
It was so funny.
那太搞笑了。

378
00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:17.930
She wanted me off camera when she knows Helen's dead for Helen's death.
她想让我出现在镜头外，因为她知道海伦（Helen）在海伦之死那场戏里已经死了。

379
00:17:18.630 --> 00:17:18.810
Yeah.
是啊。

380
00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:25.430
And so, they called me up after I rapped and they said, Sandy, you know, was wondering if you could maybe come back and do that.
所以，在我杀青后他们给我打电话，说桑迪想知道我能不能回去补拍那个镜头。

381
00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:27.370
So, of course, you know, I was thrilled to go back.
当然，我当时非常高兴能回去。

382
00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:28.690
But anyway, I came back.
总之，我回去了。

383
00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:32.850
And so, I'm in the bus and Keanu gets on the bus and he said, what are you doing here?
我坐在公交车上，基努（Keanu）上了车，他问我，你在这里干什么？

384
00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:33.510
You're dead.
你不是死了吗？

385
00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:36.170
I said, off camera.
我说，在镜头外。

386
00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:38.690
Yeah.
没错。

387
00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:42.170
Have you stayed close with any of your bus mates after this experience?
在这段经历之后，你和车上的其他伙伴还有保持密切联系吗？

388
00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:44.630
I know it's been 30 years, but –
我知道已经过去30年了，但是——

389
00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:44.830
Yeah.
有。

390
00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:46.730
Sandy's the only one.
只有桑迪。

391
00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:55.610
And since she is a very wonderful mother and very much engaged in her life, you know, as a mom, I haven't seen her as much.
因为她现在是一位非常棒的母亲，生活重心都在孩子身上，所以我们见面的机会没那么多了。

392
00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:59.770
We've had some email exchanges, but I haven't seen her for a while.
我们偶尔会发邮件交流，但我已经有一阵子没见到她了。

393
00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:02.610
But we were very close for a long time.
不过我们曾有很长一段时间非常亲密。

394
00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:05.710
And, you know, I would still call her if I needed help.
而且，你知道，如果我需要帮助，我还是会给她打电话。

395
00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:09.850
If I was – something was going on and it was urgent, I wouldn't hesitate to call her.
如果我遇到了什么紧急情况，我绝对会毫不犹豫地打给她。

396
00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:10.390
I love her.
我爱她。

397
00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:14.230
Now, I know she would respond, you know, and I hope she knows that about me.
我知道她一定会回应我，也希望她知道我也会这样对她。

398
00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:17.950
So, yeah, it was a lifelong friendship developed with her.
所以，是的，我和她建立了一生的友谊。

399
00:18:18.230 --> 00:18:19.490
That's so wonderful.
那真是太棒了。

400
00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:20.310
Yeah.
是啊。

401
00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:23.530
And so, we reunited on Time to Kill.
就这样，我们在《杀戮时刻》里重聚了。

402
00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:28.770
And then she wrote – during that period, she wrote a little short called Making Sandwiches.
后来她写了——在那期间，她写了一部名为《制作三明治》的短片。

403
00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:35.330
And she wrote a part – I don't know if she wrote it for me or if I just happened to be lucky and be there at the right time to play it.
她写了一个角色——我不知道她是专门为我写的，还是我刚好足够幸运，在合适的时间出现在那里并出演了这个角色。

404
00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:37.310
But we shot it in Ventura.
但我们是在文图拉拍摄的。

405
00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:38.010
It's a little short.
那是一部小短片。

406
00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.690
Octavia Spencer's in it.
奥克塔维亚·斯宾瑟参演了。

407
00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:42.010
Matthew McConaughey's in it.
马修·麦康纳也参演了。

408
00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:42.850
Me.
还有我。

409
00:18:43.090 --> 00:18:46.170
Oh, Eric Roberts is in it.
哦，埃里克·罗伯茨也参演了。

410
00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:49.430
That's quite the cast for a short film.
对于一部短片来说，这阵容相当强大。

411
00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:50.070
Yeah.
是啊。

412
00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:55.910
It premiered at Sundance and, you know, wonderful little movie.
它在圣丹斯电影节首映，你知道的，那是一部很棒的小电影。

413
00:18:56.230 --> 00:19:02.750
Then when All About Steve came along, my agent said, you need to get in there and play her mother.
后来当《关于史蒂夫的一切》筹拍时，我的经纪人说，你得去争取演她妈妈。

414
00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:06.370
But it was written as an aging Marilyn Monroe type.
但剧本里写的是一个老去的玛丽莲·梦露式的角色。

415
00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:09.090
And I'm thinking, that's not my casting.
我在想，这不符合我的戏路。

416
00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:12.850
But my agent was just like, I want you on that movie.
但我的经纪人坚持说，我希望你接那部电影。

417
00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:16.050
And so, she got me the audition.
于是，她帮我争取到了试镜机会。

418
00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:17.950
I said, okay, I'm going for it.
我说，好吧，我豁出去了。

419
00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:23.590
And so, I wore this pink fluffy dress, put on a blonde wig, and went in and went for it.
于是，我穿上一件粉色的蓬蓬裙，戴上金发假发，就去试镜了。

420
00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:28.870
And then Sandy called me to tell me that I got it, that the studio approved me.
后来桑迪打电话告诉我，我被选上了，制片方认可了我。

421
00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:32.650
And it was just thrilling to then go get to play her mom.
能去演她妈妈真是太让人兴奋了。

422
00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:33.790
We had the best time.
我们度过了一段最美好的时光。

423
00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:35.030
And we laughed so much.
我们笑得特别开心。

424
00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:41.130
And it was so fun for me to play a character like that because no one in the world would believe I would do it.
能演这样一个角色对我来说太有趣了，因为全世界都不会相信我会去演这种角色。

425
00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:46.990
But it just goes to show you really need to go for it, you know, if you audition.
但这恰恰说明，如果你去试镜，真的需要放手一搏。

426
00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:56.350
I mean, if I had said offer only or if I hadn't been willing to take a chance, you know, I really, it wouldn't have happened.
我是说，如果我当时坚持只接邀约角色，或者我不愿意冒险尝试，你知道的，这一切都不会发生。

427
00:19:56.650 --> 00:20:08.550
So, Beth, you've done three films with Sandra Bullock, plus you were in her directorial debut and only film she's ever directed.
贝丝，你和桑德拉·布洛克合作了三部电影，还参演了她导演处女作，也是她唯一执导过的电影。

428
00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:09.610
So far.
目前为止是这样。

429
00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:18.430
So, you've, you guys have worked together over these 30 years since Speed, four times in these different movies and have a lifelong friendship.
所以，自《生死时速》以来的这30年里，你们在这些不同的电影中合作了四次，并建立了终身的友谊。

430
00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:19.450
Yeah.
是的。

431
00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.410
I mean, what a blessing.
我是说，这真是种福气。

432
00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:22.430
This movie.
这部电影。

433
00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:23.530
Yeah.
是啊。

434
00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:25.310
Yeah, it is.
没错，确实是。

435
00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:25.650
It is.
确实。

436
00:20:25.710 --> 00:20:26.850
It's what you take with you.
这才是你最终收获的东西。

437
00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:29.310
In the end, that's what it's all about.
归根结底，这才是最重要的。

438
00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:29.830
Yeah.
是啊。

439
00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:37.210
Well, you know, she did me, I mean, she saved, I told her this and, you know, she never wants to take credit for anything.
嗯，你知道，她对我……我是说，她救了……我告诉过她这件事，你知道的，她从不愿居功。

440
00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:41.330
She always compliments everybody else and is always so giving and loving.
她总是称赞别人，总是那么慷慨和充满爱心。

441
00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:45.290
And, but she saved my life on that movie.
但是，她在拍那部电影时救了我的命。

442
00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:50.930
First of all, I don't know that I would have stayed on the movie once I saw that thing, but I had bonded with her.
首先，我不知道如果我看到那东西（拍摄环境）后还会不会留在剧组，但我已经和她建立了深厚的感情。

443
00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:51.950
I loved her.
我爱她。

444
00:20:52.290 --> 00:21:03.130
You know, I felt like I wanted to work with her and Keanu and Jan gave me, but beyond that, she just was always upbeat and positive.
你知道，我觉得我想和她还有基努合作，简给了我机会，但除此之外，她总是那么乐观积极。

445
00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:11.930
She had such a good attitude and we had chocolate break every day at, I think, four o'clock and they would bring out the chocolate.
她的态度非常好，我们每天下午四点左右都有巧克力休息时间，他们会把巧克力拿出来。

446
00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:16.030
And we would, and I didn't even eat sugar at the time, but honey, I was eating Tootsie Rolls.
我们就会……那时我甚至不吃糖，但亲爱的，我当时一直在吃图西卷糖。

447
00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:20.770
And we would dance, if you can believe it.
我们还会跳舞，你敢信吗？

448
00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:30.250
We would put on salsa music and she's a great dancer and she would salsa dance, you know, my pitiful version of salsa dancing.
我们会放萨尔萨舞曲，她跳舞很棒，她会跳萨尔萨，而我跳的是那种笨拙的版本，你知道的。

449
00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:36.870
But she kept everybody going, like if it was, cause it was so hot and the hours were so long.
但她让每个人都保持动力，因为当时天气太热了，工作时间又那么长。

450
00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:39.370
And as I say, we couldn't even get to our trailers, all of that.
正如我所说，我们甚至都无法回到自己的拖车里，诸如此类的事情。

451
00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:46.770
But her attitude was so good and positive and loving at all times that she kept me going.
但她始终保持着积极、乐观、充满爱心的态度，这支撑着我走下去。

452
00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:48.530
I mean, I made it because of her.
我是说，我能成功全靠她。

453
00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:52.370
And so I really feel like, you know, I owe her that forever.
所以我真的觉得，你知道，我永远欠她这份情。

454
00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:58.210
So while you were shooting it, you knew, you knew this was going to be a hit while you were making it.
所以当你们在拍摄的时候，你们就知道，你们在制作的时候就知道这会是一部热门作品。

455
00:21:58.310 --> 00:21:59.370
You guys felt it.
你们感觉到了。

456
00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:01.330
You could feel you were part of something special.
你们能感觉到自己参与了一部特别的作品。

457
00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:02.250
We could.
我们确实感觉到了。

458
00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:06.950
I mean, also, it just felt good.
我是说，而且，感觉真的很棒。

459
00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:10.610
You know, Jan was on his game.
你知道，简当时状态极佳。

460
00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:12.670
The crew was on their game.
剧组人员也都表现得非常出色。

461
00:22:13.490 --> 00:22:16.950
Keanu, I could see, was going to be an action star.
我当时就能看出，基努会成为一名动作巨星。

462
00:22:17.090 --> 00:22:18.290
It worked out pretty well.
结果确实非常成功。

463
00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:19.650
Sure did.
确实如此。

464
00:22:20.070 --> 00:22:20.410
Yeah.
是的。

465
00:22:21.590 --> 00:22:23.830
And you just could tell.
你一眼就能看出来。

466
00:22:24.210 --> 00:22:26.050
And he was so sweet.
而且他非常贴心。

467
00:22:26.350 --> 00:22:27.450
Talk about bonding.
说到建立感情。

468
00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:28.070
Yeah.
是的。

469
00:22:28.190 --> 00:22:29.750
Can we talk a little bit about Keanu?
我们能聊聊基努吗？

470
00:22:30.310 --> 00:22:30.990
Oh, my God.
天哪。

471
00:22:31.010 --> 00:22:32.090
I want to tell you everything.
我什么都想告诉你。

472
00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:39.610
One day in Long Beach, I guess it was the day, in fact, we did that thing on the on-ramp where we ran into the water barrels.
有一天在长滩，我想就是那天，事实上，我们拍了那个在匝道上撞上水桶的戏。

473
00:22:39.970 --> 00:22:40.170
Sure.
当然。

474
00:22:40.370 --> 00:22:41.210
That was what we were shooting.
那就是我们当时在拍的戏。

475
00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:42.870
So there's a lot of technical stuff to work out.
所以有很多技术性的东西需要解决。

476
00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:45.970
So we had a lot of downtime on the streets of Long Beach.
因此我们在长滩的街道上有不少空闲时间。

477
00:22:45.970 --> 00:22:56.890
And so we made up a comedy show that would be called Sandy, Sandy, kind of cute, kind of wild, Sandy.
于是我们编了一个喜剧节目，叫《桑迪，桑迪》，有点可爱，有点狂野，桑迪。

478
00:22:57.590 --> 00:22:59.790
And then he would be the boyfriend.
然后他扮演男朋友。

479
00:22:59.790 --> 00:23:01.170
And I don't know.
我也不知道。

480
00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:03.970
I think I was making it up and he was acting it out.
我想是我在编，而他在表演。

481
00:23:04.030 --> 00:23:15.490
And he fell on the grass and kicked like a cockroach and just did, I mean, just cute, funny stuff that you don't really see that side of him, you know,
他倒在草地上，像只蟑螂一样乱蹬，真的，就是那种可爱、搞笑的举动，你平时真的很难看到他那一面，你知道的，

482
00:23:15.590 --> 00:23:18.070
very often in interviews or in what he does.
在采访中或者他的作品里并不常见。

483
00:23:18.070 --> 00:23:23.590
But just cute, sweet, funny, going with whatever crazy game we were coming up with.
但他就是那么可爱、贴心、风趣，配合着我们想出的任何疯狂游戏。

484
00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:26.670
And just such a team player with his caSt.
而且他作为搭档真的非常有团队精神。

485
00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:28.470
That sounds so charming.
听起来太迷人了。

486
00:23:28.610 --> 00:23:33.590
I feel like we were like that on the set of The Office, Jenna, how we would get punchy being in the conference room.
我觉得我们在《办公室》片场也是这样，珍娜，我们在会议室里待久了也会变得很亢奋。

487
00:23:33.730 --> 00:23:35.250
Listen, it wasn't a moving bus.
听着，那又不是一辆行驶中的公交车。

488
00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:37.910
We didn't have to hang out on the side of a freeway.
我们不需要挂在高速公路边上。

489
00:23:38.050 --> 00:23:47.950
But we definitely had all of these little comedy bits we would do and and act out and be silly and kept us going through like long days on set.
但我们确实有很多小段子，我们会表演出来，搞搞怪，这支撑着我们度过片场漫长的一天。

490
00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:49.430
That's why it worked.
这就是它成功的原因。

491
00:23:49.710 --> 00:23:53.010
You know, you can feel it on that show.
你知道，在那部剧里你能感觉到这一点。

492
00:23:53.170 --> 00:23:54.010
You really can.
真的能感觉到。

493
00:23:54.250 --> 00:23:56.050
I mean, your show and that show.
我是说，你的剧和那部剧都是。

494
00:23:56.950 --> 00:23:57.950
But you can.
但你确实能感觉到。

495
00:23:58.070 --> 00:23:58.790
You can feel it.
你能感觉到。

496
00:23:59.070 --> 00:24:00.950
It just couldn't have worked any other way.
它不可能以其他任何方式成功。

497
00:24:01.050 --> 00:24:04.130
I love the idea of thinking that Keanu does bits.
一想到基努会演小段子，我就觉得很有趣。

498
00:24:05.470 --> 00:24:06.030
Exactly.
没错。

499
00:24:06.970 --> 00:24:13.810
Beth, I have to know, was there ever like a stunt that went wrong for a second?
贝丝，我必须得问问，有没有哪次特技表演出现过瞬间的失误？

500
00:24:14.230 --> 00:24:16.690
Were there any mishaps that you remember?
你还记得有什么意外吗？

501
00:24:16.690 --> 00:24:18.510
Or was it all pretty controlled?
还是说一切都在掌控之中？

502
00:24:21.060 --> 00:24:26.800
I can't remember anything going wrong except, you know, maybe my acting.
我不记得有什么出错，除了，你知道，可能我的演技吧。

503
00:24:27.880 --> 00:24:28.800
Oh, no.
噢，不。

504
00:24:29.960 --> 00:24:30.920
My whining.
我的抱怨。

505
00:24:31.400 --> 00:24:37.380
I tell you, I went to that premiere and I thought, get that lady off the bus with her whining.
我跟你说，我去参加首映礼的时候心想，快让那个满嘴抱怨的女人下车吧。

506
00:24:37.600 --> 00:24:38.740
What about the rest of us?
那我们其他人呢？

507
00:24:38.820 --> 00:24:40.020
What about the rest of us?
那我们其他人呢？

508
00:24:40.440 --> 00:24:44.440
You know, Jan said to me, I asked him, I said, why aren't I the hero anymore?
你知道，简跟我说，我问他，我说，为什么我不再是英雄了？

509
00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:45.580
Of course, we have too many heroes.
当然，我们的英雄太多了。

510
00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:49.120
He said, we need Richard Chamberlain in Towering Inferno.
他说，我们需要《火烧摩天楼》里的理查德·张伯伦。

511
00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:50.120
We need a coward.
我们需要一个懦夫。

512
00:24:52.860 --> 00:24:54.360
So I was the coward.
所以我成了那个懦夫。

513
00:24:54.820 --> 00:24:57.960
But in the original script, Jeff Daniels was the bad guy.
但在最初的剧本里，杰夫·丹尼尔斯才是那个坏蛋。

514
00:24:57.960 --> 00:24:58.720
Yes.
没错。

515
00:24:59.500 --> 00:25:00.620
Isn't that shocking?
这不令人震惊吗？

516
00:25:00.920 --> 00:25:01.080
Yeah.
是啊。

517
00:25:01.480 --> 00:25:02.740
He was in cahoots.
他当时是同谋。

518
00:25:03.020 --> 00:25:03.200
Yeah.
是啊。

519
00:25:03.200 --> 00:25:04.320
It was really good.
真的很棒。

520
00:25:04.800 --> 00:25:05.200
It was.
确实。

521
00:25:05.400 --> 00:25:06.020
I liked it.
我很喜欢。

522
00:25:06.020 --> 00:25:07.240
You liked that twiSt.
你喜欢那个反转。

523
00:25:07.600 --> 00:25:08.140
I did.
我喜欢。

524
00:25:08.340 --> 00:25:12.940
But I also thought that it was very moving when he died in our version.
但我也觉得他在我们这个版本里死的时候非常感人。

525
00:25:13.160 --> 00:25:13.600
Me too.
我也是。

526
00:25:14.240 --> 00:25:19.700
I did think that worked very well because that second on his face when he knows he's going
我确实觉得那段处理得很好，因为他脸上那一瞬间的表情，当他知道自己要

527
00:25:19.700 --> 00:25:20.080
to die.
死的时候。

528
00:25:20.620 --> 00:25:21.640
Oh, my God.
天哪。

529
00:25:22.440 --> 00:25:24.120
And who doesn't love Jeff Daniels?
而且谁能不喜欢杰夫·丹尼尔斯呢？

530
00:25:24.660 --> 00:25:26.080
You know what's crazy?
你知道最疯狂的是什么吗？

531
00:25:26.240 --> 00:25:31.720
After I watched that scene and I saw that moment of realization in his eyes after he sees the
看完那场戏，看到他看到红灯后眼中那一瞬间的领悟，我看了好几遍，然后试着把它当作表演练习来做。

532
00:25:31.720 --> 00:25:37.820
red light, I watched it several times and then I tried to do it as an acting exercise.
我也试了，我也试了。

533
00:25:38.080 --> 00:25:38.920
I did too, too.
我还没到能演出杰夫·丹尼尔斯那种领悟时刻的程度。

534
00:25:42.190 --> 00:25:47.550
Enough actor that I could do Jeff Daniels' moment of realization.
那真的太棒了。

535
00:25:48.090 --> 00:25:49.630
It was so good.
所以我试了一下。

536
00:25:49.770 --> 00:25:50.830
So I tried it.
这太搞笑了。

537
00:25:50.930 --> 00:25:51.490
This is so funny.
我也做了同样的事。

538
00:25:51.650 --> 00:25:52.970
I did the same thing.
我说，我能做到吗？

539
00:25:53.190 --> 00:25:54.370
I said, could I do that?
看起来会真实吗？

540
00:25:54.570 --> 00:25:55.490
Would it look real?
我看起来像个卡通人物吗？

541
00:25:55.490 --> 00:25:56.650
Do I look like a cartoon?
是的，因为那真的太棒了。

542
00:25:57.170 --> 00:26:00.390
Yes, it was so because it was so good.
好吧，我为你们感到骄傲。

543
00:26:00.830 --> 00:26:02.950
Well, I'm proud of you guys.
只有真正的演员才会那样做。

544
00:26:03.190 --> 00:26:06.050
Those are real actors that would do that.
你们看到了一个伟大的瞬间，就想看看自己能不能复刻它。

545
00:26:06.290 --> 00:26:10.130
You saw a great moment and you wanted to see if you could duplicate it.
我毫不怀疑你们能做到，而且做得很好。

546
00:26:10.210 --> 00:26:12.250
And I have no doubt that you would and good.
那太棒了。

547
00:26:13.050 --> 00:26:14.010
That's great.
我演得有点像卡通片。

548
00:26:14.450 --> 00:26:15.950
Mine was a little cartoony.
我可不是杰夫·丹尼尔斯。

549
00:26:16.270 --> 00:26:17.630
I'm no Jeff Daniels.
我得说。

550
00:26:17.750 --> 00:26:18.430
I'll say that.
我得说。

551
00:26:18.590 --> 00:26:19.570
But my goodness.
天哪。

552
00:26:20.530 --> 00:26:24.990
It's crazy, though, because so many people in the film did not get to work together.
不过这真的很疯狂，因为电影里很多人根本没机会一起合作。

553
00:26:24.990 --> 00:26:27.390
They're like, you never got to work with Jeff Daniels.
他们会说，你没能和杰夫·丹尼尔斯合作。

554
00:26:27.510 --> 00:26:29.090
You never got to work with Dennis Hopper.
你没能和丹尼斯·霍珀合作。

555
00:26:30.930 --> 00:26:33.910
Dennis Hopper was by himself for most of the movie.
丹尼斯·霍珀在电影里大部分时间都是独自一人。

556
00:26:34.250 --> 00:26:34.830
On a telephone.
在电话那头。

557
00:26:35.710 --> 00:26:46.250
But, you know, one thing that I did notice on the bus, which just blew my mind, is how you've got, you know, the police captain and all the police officers are on like a flatbed.
但你知道，我在巴士上注意到的一件事让我大为震惊，就是警察队长和所有警官都待在平板拖车上。

558
00:26:46.250 --> 00:26:48.250
Next to the bus.
就在巴士旁边。

559
00:26:48.490 --> 00:26:54.570
And there are all these scenes where they are just the background of something that's happening on the bus.
有很多场景里，他们只是巴士上发生的事情的背景。

560
00:26:54.710 --> 00:27:00.190
Did those guys just ride next to you for 12 hours a day sometimes?
那些人有时真的要在你旁边坐上12个小时吗？

561
00:27:00.730 --> 00:27:01.710
That was crazy.
那太疯狂了。

562
00:27:02.130 --> 00:27:03.530
In the heat on a flatbed?
在那种高温下待在平板拖车上？

563
00:27:03.950 --> 00:27:04.310
I know.
我知道。

564
00:27:04.450 --> 00:27:06.570
In those SWAT uniforms or whatever.
穿着那些特警制服之类的。

565
00:27:06.890 --> 00:27:10.650
Those heavy duty, you know, with the bulletproof veSt.
那些厚重的装备，还有防弹背心。

566
00:27:10.650 --> 00:27:12.950
Well, you know, stunt guys, you know, stunt guys.
嗯，你知道的，特技演员嘛，特技演员。

567
00:27:13.170 --> 00:27:15.930
I mean, they are just gluttons for punishment, I guess.
我的意思是，我想他们就是那种自讨苦吃的人。

568
00:27:16.250 --> 00:27:16.950
I don't know.
我不知道。

569
00:27:17.270 --> 00:27:18.450
They're amazing.
他们太棒了。

570
00:27:18.870 --> 00:27:22.350
I mean, and they seem to take great joy in it.
我的意思是，他们似乎乐在其中。

571
00:27:22.490 --> 00:27:23.510
I mean, I'm sure they're nice.
我是说，我相信他们人很好。

572
00:27:23.670 --> 00:27:25.710
They go home and they say, I'm never doing this again.
他们回家时会说，我再也不干这个了。

573
00:27:25.810 --> 00:27:28.890
But it's not my experience with stunt people.
但这并不是我与特技演员相处的经历。

574
00:27:29.050 --> 00:27:32.870
They are always so enthusiastic and ready for action.
他们总是那么热情，随时准备行动。

575
00:27:32.870 --> 00:27:35.350
But they are really phenomenal.
但他们真的很了不起。

576
00:27:35.730 --> 00:27:39.170
I mean, they just always just are so eager to jump into the fray.
我的意思是，他们总是那么渴望投入到激烈的战斗中。

577
00:27:40.390 --> 00:27:42.010
And God bless them.
愿上帝保佑他们。

578
00:27:42.290 --> 00:27:43.790
I mean, we need them.
我的意思是，我们需要他们。

579
00:27:44.250 --> 00:27:45.110
That's for sure.
那是肯定的。

580
00:27:45.350 --> 00:27:46.070
Yeah, we sure do.
是的，我们确实需要。

581
00:27:46.410 --> 00:27:48.530
And every step person on speed.
还有《生死时速》里的每一位特技演员。

582
00:27:48.650 --> 00:27:49.350
But yeah, they were there on that flatbed.
但没错，他们当时就在那辆平板拖车上。

583
00:27:49.510 --> 00:27:49.690
Yeah.
是的。

584
00:27:49.890 --> 00:27:51.510
Suffering in the heat.
在高温中受苦。

585
00:27:51.670 --> 00:27:53.470
And it was hot, hot, hot.
而且当时真的很热、很热、很热。

586
00:27:53.750 --> 00:27:58.050
You know, September in California, Southern California is hotter than the summer.
你知道，加州的九月，南加州比夏天还要热。

587
00:27:58.610 --> 00:28:00.570
And it was, yeah, God bless them.
确实，愿上帝保佑他们。

588
00:28:00.570 --> 00:28:02.870
It's our hottest month for sure, is September.
九月绝对是我们最热的月份。

589
00:28:02.870 --> 00:28:04.090
I think so too, yeah.
我也这么认为，没错。

590
00:28:04.130 --> 00:28:04.270
Yeah.
是的。

591
00:28:04.650 --> 00:28:05.830
Definitely was that year.
那一年绝对是这样。

592
00:28:06.430 --> 00:28:10.350
Well, you know, Beth, you have been in so many things.
嗯，贝丝，你演过太多作品了。

593
00:28:10.350 --> 00:28:11.990
And we've talked about a few of them here.
我们在这里也聊过其中几部。

594
00:28:12.250 --> 00:28:15.370
I'm personally with my daughter re-watching The Mindy Project.
我个人正和我女儿重温《明迪烦事多》。

595
00:28:15.390 --> 00:28:17.470
And you are hilarious in it.
你在里面太搞笑了。

596
00:28:17.830 --> 00:28:21.590
She was like, Mom, please tell Beth how much we love her in The Mindy Project.
她说，妈妈，请告诉贝丝我们有多喜欢她在《明迪烦事多》里的表现。

597
00:28:21.650 --> 00:28:22.630
So I said I would.
所以我答应了她。

598
00:28:23.070 --> 00:28:24.190
Oh, tell her.
哦，替我谢谢她。

599
00:28:24.330 --> 00:28:25.290
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

600
00:28:25.430 --> 00:28:25.870
Yes.
是的。

601
00:28:26.050 --> 00:28:29.770
But we are curious, what do you get recognized the most for?
不过我们很好奇，大家最常因为什么角色认出你来？

602
00:28:29.770 --> 00:28:33.410
Is there a character that people really identify with when you're out in the world?
当你走在外面时，有没有哪个角色是大家特别有共鸣的？

603
00:28:34.430 --> 00:28:41.150
Well, you know, what I found is, obviously, it depends on, you know, the fans of which thing.
嗯，你知道，我发现这显然取决于粉丝们喜欢的是哪部作品。

604
00:28:41.610 --> 00:28:44.050
Like, it's speed fans, it's speed.
比如，如果是《生死时速》的粉丝，那就是《生死时速》。

605
00:28:44.310 --> 00:28:46.730
But I will, you're going to think I'm making it up.
但我接下来说的，你可能会觉得我在编故事。

606
00:28:46.870 --> 00:28:50.210
But I promise you that The Office is at the top, top, tippy top.
但我向你保证，《办公室》绝对是排在最顶端、最顶端、顶尖中的顶尖。

607
00:28:50.770 --> 00:28:53.210
You know, people love that show so much.
你知道，人们真的非常喜欢那部剧。

608
00:28:53.370 --> 00:28:55.210
They love the dinner party episode.
他们特别喜欢“晚宴”那一集。

609
00:28:55.210 --> 00:28:59.210
I mean, a lot of people have called and gotten interviews with me.
我是说，很多人都打来电话，希望能采访我。

